WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.161
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 7: Let's Go!

2
00:00:03.241 --> 00:00:07.266
In this unit you will learn how we travel and get around.

3
00:00:07.346 --> 00:00:15.764
You will meet the words for ways to travel — walk, bus, car,
bicycle and boat — and learn to say how you go to school.

4
00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:23.541
You will talk about journeys: going somewhere with the
people you love, staying safe, and enjoying the trip.

5
00:00:23.621 --> 00:00:29.879
Say the words out loud — this is about
confident everyday English, not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:29.959 --> 00:00:35.928
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:36.008 --> 00:00:44.999
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
ways to travel (walk, bus, car, bicycle, boat, train, plane).

8
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:50.072
You will also say how they get to
school: “I go to school by ___.”

9
00:00:50.152 --> 00:00:56.068
You will also say the action words for
travel (drive, ride, fly, float, walk).

10
00:00:56.148 --> 00:00:58.912
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:04.094
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: walk, bus, car, bicycle, boat, train.

12
00:01:04.174 --> 00:01:09.152
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

13
00:01:09.232 --> 00:01:13.085
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

14
00:01:13.165 --> 00:01:17.465
The reading sequence includes Amal's
Big Bus Ride and Talk about Let's Go!.

15
00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:18.283
Read actively.

16
00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:22.313
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

17
00:01:22.393 --> 00:01:26.109
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

18
00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:29.308
The first language focus is Say how you travel.

19
00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:32.235
Tell us how you get to school each morning.

20
00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:35.162
Say the way you travel after the word 'by'.

21
00:01:35.242 --> 00:01:42.581
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

22
00:01:42.661 --> 00:01:46.408
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:50.612
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

24
00:01:50.692 --> 00:01:53.812
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

25
00:01:53.892 --> 00:01:57.137
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

26
00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.642
You are ready to begin.

27
00:01:58.722 --> 00:02:05.120
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

28
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.261
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

29
00:02:08.341 --> 00:02:15.525
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
